  "protocolVersion": null,
  "instructions": "Templated renders images (PNG, JPG, WebP), multi-page PDFs and MP4 videos from templates: it fills a saved design with the given text, images and colors (template rendering, not AI image generation).\nThe usual flow is list_templates to find a template, get_template_layers to read its layer names, then create_render with those names as the keys of layers. If a layer name doesn't exist in the template, create_render renders nothing and returns the valid names.\nWhen the account has no templates yet (common right after sign-up), create_template can design one from the user's description, so a first render doesn't require the Templated web app.\nFor batches, rendering one item and checking the result before rendering the rest avoids repeating a layout problem across many renders.\nCommon sizes: Instagram post 1080x1080, story 1080x1920, link preview (OG) 1200x630, A4 landscape certificate 1754x1240.",
  "durationMs": 5828,
  "stderr": "Templated MCP server running on stdio\n"
}
